# ESP32-S3 boards with 8 MB octal PSRAM (ESP32-S3R8 chip, e.g. N16R8 modules on
# DevKitC-style boards with two USB-C ports). For D6, A/B are mounted in
# screw-terminal expansion plates and C is bare. This overlay changes the
# PSRAM mode only: the base build still uses its 4 MB partition layout.
# Use: BOARD=n16r8 NODE=<id> PORT=<port> sh tools/mtk.sh flash, with the
# cable in the port wired to the chip's own USB (the console is USB-Serial-JTAG),
# not the one through the CH343 UART bridge.
# CONFIG_SPIRAM_MODE_QUAD is not set
CONFIG_SPIRAM_MODE_OCT=y
